</script>

# Button Group

Joins related buttons into one control. Inner corners turn square and neighbors share a border. Inputs, selects, and other controls can join too.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { ButtonGroup } from "#lib/components/ui/button-group/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<ButtonGroup aria-label="Message actions">
	<Button variant="outline">Archive</Button>
	<Button variant="outline">Report</Button>
	<Button variant="outline">Snooze</Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/button-group.json
```

## Accessibility

`ButtonGroup` renders a `div` with `role="group"`. Give it an `aria-label` that names the set of actions. Each button keeps its own place in the tab order.

## Vertical

Set `orientation="vertical"` to stack the children.

<Demo section="vertical" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup orientation="vertical" aria-label="Zoom">
	<Button variant="outline" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Zoom in"><PlusIcon /></Button>
	<Button variant="outline" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Zoom out"><MinusIcon /></Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Nested

Place groups inside a group to keep them apart with a gap, such as pagination arrows beside page numbers.

<Demo section="nested" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup>
	<ButtonGroup>...</ButtonGroup>
	<ButtonGroup>...</ButtonGroup>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Separator

Outline buttons share a visible border, but filled buttons do not. Place `ButtonGroupSeparator` between filled buttons that share a color, such as two `secondary` buttons.

<Demo section="separator" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup>
	<Button variant="secondary">Copy</Button>
	<ButtonGroupSeparator />
	<Button variant="secondary" size="icon-md" aria-label="Copy options"><CopyIcon /></Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## With input

An `Input` inside the group fills the room left by the buttons.

<Demo section="input" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup>
	<Input placeholder="Search..." />
	<Button variant="outline" aria-label="Search"><SearchIcon /></Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Text

Place `ButtonGroupText` to join static text, such as a prefix or a unit. Set its `size` to match the buttons.

<Demo section="text" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup>
	<ButtonGroupText>https://</ButtonGroupText>
	<Input placeholder="example.com" />
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Sizes

The group has no size of its own, so set the same `size` on each part: `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. `ButtonGroupText` defaults to `md`, like the buttons and inputs.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ButtonGroup>
	<ButtonGroupText size="sm">https://</ButtonGroupText>
	<Input size="sm" placeholder="example.com" />
	<Button variant="outline" size="sm">Go</Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## API

`ButtonGroup`, `ButtonGroupSeparator`, and `ButtonGroupText` extend the native `div` attributes. The group has no size of its own; size the buttons inside it instead.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Direction the children are joined in; defaults to `horizontal` */
	orientation?: "horizontal" | "vertical";
}

interface SeparatorProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Matches the group direction; `vertical` for a horizontal group; defaults to `vertical` */
	orientation?: "horizontal" | "vertical";
}

interface TextProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Height, padding, and text size on the shared scale; match it to the buttons; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}
```
